SRR3106225	PRJNA309357	SRP068730	SAMN04421844	SRX1534653	Mus musculus	E10.5 PGC WGBS Replicate 1	E10.5 PGC WGBS Replicate 1	Illumina HiSeq 2000 sequencing: GSM2041731: E10.5 PGC WGBS Replicate 1 Mus musculus Bisulfite-Seq	Bisulfite-Seq	GENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED	ILLUMINA	Illumina HiSeq 2000	Total DNA was isolated from 10,000 sorted PGCs using the QIAamp DNA Micro Kit (Qiagen) with 0.8 µg of carrier RNA and following the “Isolating DNA from small samples of blood” protocol. In some cases, unmethylated λ phage DNA (Promega) was spiked in following DNA isolation to assess bisulphite conversion rate. DNA was fragmented using a Covaris S2 sonicator (Covaris), as per manufacturer’s instructions. Libraries were made following the NEBNext Library Prep protocol, with the following modifications: 1) methylated adaptors were diluted 1:10 in nuclease free H2O to a final concentration of 1.5 µM 2) following adaptor ligation, bisulphite conversion was carried out using the Imprint Modification Kit (Sigma), and following the two step protocol according to the manufacturer’s specifications and 3) PCR enrichment was carried out for 16 cycles using the NEXTflex Bisulphite-Seq Kit for Illumina Sequencing (Bioo Scientific) master mix and the NEBNext Library Prep universal and index primers (NEB). The libraries were purified by AMPure XP beads (Beckman-Coulter). Libraries were sequenced on the Illumina HiSeq 2000 or 2500 instrument.	354803535	70960707000	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR310/005/SRR3106225/SRR3106225_1.fastq.gz;ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR310/005/SRR3106225/SRR3106225_2.fastq.gz	f98185e1a151ce12e82b6bfce0ce3371;a554b4c4318171b2af55211e44ee557e	26421725382;24639249065
